{"study_accession":"PRJNA646628","secondary_study_accession":"SRP272195","title":"Blood-Tumor overlapping TCR repertoire predicts the clinical responses of PD-1 blockade in patients with gastrointestinal cancer[RNA-Seq]","description":"As the anti-PD-1 monoclonal antibody (mAb) becomes to be used in many types of cancers, the needs for the predictive biomarker of PD-1 blockade are growing. T cell receptor (TCR) repertoire—which reflects the anti-tumor T-cell responses based on the antigen specificity—is a potential biomarker of cancer immunotherapy. Here, we analyzed the TCR repertoire of patients with advanced gastrointestinal cancer and explored its association with clinical responses. Overall design: Eight patients with advanced gastrointestinal cancer were treated with an anti-PD-1 monoclonal antibody (nivolumab) every 3 weeks until disease progression. The TCR repertoire of the peripheral blood CD4+ and CD8+ T cells was analyzed once before and three times after the initiation of treatment, whereas in case of tumor biopsy it was analyzed before and after 6 weeks of initiation of the treatment.","pubmed":"34014607","geo_series":"","n_samples":26,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN15548463","study_accession":"PRJNA646628","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"study","title":"RNA_P1_Tumor_2_0011","description":"RNA_P1_Tumor_2_0011","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM4673108","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-07-20","attributes":[["source_name","tumor biopsy"],["age","80"],["sex","male"],["cancer type","esophageal"],["tissue","tumor biopsy"],["date","0"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR12234317","experiment_accession":"SRX8742777","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Ion Torrent S5","read_count":1692420,"base_count":183448135,"first_public":"2021-07-20","experiment_title":"Ion Torrent S5 sequencing: GSM4673108: RNA_P1_Tumor_2_0011 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":